From: cybercluster <noreply@thenortonfamily.net>
Subject: [PATCH] aic8800: let wlan0 switch to monitor mode (change_iface guard tested the wrong vif)

rwnx_cfg80211_change_iface() refused every managed->monitor switch with -EIO
because its MON_DATA guard checked RWNX_VIF_TYPE(vif) instead of vif_el, and
the driver's own P2P device vif is always in the list. Test the other vif;
skip monitor / P2P-device / down vifs. Verified on a7s-3 (radiotap capture on
channels 1-165, hand-back to managed works). a7s-linux-drivers PR #3.

--- a/bsp/drivers/net/wireless/aic8800/usb/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c	2026-09-07 22:24:51.212229925 -0400
+++ b/bsp/drivers/net/wireless/aic8800/usb/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c	2026-09-07 22:24:51.229476693 -0400
@@ -2442,13 +2442,23 @@
        (RWNX_VIF_TYPE(vif) != NL80211_IFTYPE_MONITOR)) {
         struct rwnx_vif *vif_el;
         list_for_each_entry(vif_el, &rwnx_hw->vifs, list) {
-            // Check if data interface already exists
-            if ((vif_el != vif) &&
-               (RWNX_VIF_TYPE(vif) != NL80211_IFTYPE_MONITOR)) {
-                wiphy_err(rwnx_hw->wiphy,
-                        "Monitor+Data interface support (MON_DATA) disabled\n");
-                return -EIO;
-            }
+            // Without MON_DATA firmware support a monitor interface cannot
+            // coexist with a DATA interface. Refuse only when ANOTHER
+            // interface is up and carries data (STA/AP/mesh/P2P client or GO).
+            // The P2P device wdev has no data path, and a down interface
+            // carries nothing. The original test looked at `vif` — the
+            // interface being changed — instead of `vif_el`, so the driver's
+            // own P2P device entry made every switch to monitor fail with -EIO
+            // (a7s, 2026-09-07).
+            if (vif_el == vif || !vif_el->up)
+                continue;
+            if (RWNX_VIF_TYPE(vif_el) == NL80211_IFTYPE_MONITOR ||
+                RWNX_VIF_TYPE(vif_el) == NL80211_IFTYPE_P2P_DEVICE)
+                continue;
+            wiphy_err(rwnx_hw->wiphy,
+                    "Monitor+Data interface support (MON_DATA) disabled: %s is up\n",
+                    vif_el->ndev ? vif_el->ndev->name : "an interface");
+            return -EIO;
         }
     }
 #endif
